All done — `impl` is a symlink to the round directory `impl_5`, and my changes are confined to my two files (`impl/d1_batchlane.c`, `strategies/d1_batchlane.md`; the `d1_composite.md` modification is that entry's own implementer working concurrently).

**Summary of the round:** This was an adoption round targeting my three remaining library losses, measured directly on the live a80n0 reservation (all numbers below are scoring-node, not wallaby — the reservation was alive all session). I ported d1_composite's L=60 kernels verbatim (`fft60_ymm1` for B=1/tail, `fft60_zmm2x2` for batched pairs: 60 B1 0.0687→0.047 µs, now ahead of MKL's 0.0616; 60 B512 0.0699→0.061), ported d1_pow2's L=64 in-register codelet for batched calls (64 B512 0.0657→0.044, at MKL parity), and wrote a new L=128 in-register codelet extending pow2's structure one factor up (radix-4/radix-4/radix-8, branch-grouped intermediates; interleaved A/B 0.154–0.157 vs 0.165–0.169 for the old path at B512, ~parity with MKL's 0.1584). B=1 dispatches keep my own four-step kernels at 64/128 (codelets measured a wash there). All 18 m=1 cells pass at 1.1–3.2e-16, all 12 graded chains plus odd-batch chains pass (worst 2.6e-12 vs 1e-10), output bitwise repeatable. Strategy record appended with full attributions and A/B numbers.

Technique ended on: adopted PFA ymm1/zmm2x2 at 60 (d1_composite) + in-register AoS codelets at 32/64/128 (d1_pow2 + own 128 extension) over the batch-lane SoA chain engine; best a80n0 µs/transform — B=1: 0.016 (L=13) up to 0.098 (L=128), batched: 0.010 (13) / 0.044 (31) / 0.015 (32) / 0.061 (60) / 0.044 (64) / 0.155 (128); rel L2 ≤ 3.2e-16 single-call, worst chain gate 2.6e-12 vs 1e-10.
